          "id": "aat:300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "pecia / pece (Latin, a piece): a piece used as a measure or packing unit, of definite size varying by commodity — figs (60 lb.), raisins and other fruit/citrus (a third of a sorte), Cornish tin (250 lb.) and tin foil, rosin, battery (650 lb.) and kettles, brazil, iron of Lucca, buckram, lawn, Dornix thread, saunders, hops and marmalade."
    }
  ],
